1
00:00:00,094 --> 00:00:01,294
(All characters and organisations in this drama are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,294 --> 00:00:02,434
(Filming with minors followed broadcast guidelines,)

3
00:00:02,434 --> 00:00:03,534
(and generative AI was used in select scenes.)

4
00:00:04,734 --> 00:00:06,364
- This meatball is good, isn't it? - Yes.

5
00:00:06,434 --> 00:00:07,434
What's this?

6
00:00:10,204 --> 00:00:11,274
Oh, meatballs.

7
00:00:12,604 --> 00:00:13,604
That looks delicious.

8
00:00:16,014 --> 00:00:17,274
I didn't order any for you, Father.

9
00:00:18,714 --> 00:00:20,384
We can just share.

10
00:00:21,584 --> 00:00:24,684
There's none for you guys either. I only ordered for Gyeol and me.

11
00:00:28,124 --> 00:00:30,454
From now on, do your own laundry...

12
00:00:30,954 --> 00:00:32,624
and make your own meals.

13
00:00:33,894 --> 00:00:34,894
What are you talking about?

14
00:00:34,964 --> 00:00:36,194
Are you trying to screw over the family?

15
00:00:37,364 --> 00:00:40,334
I don't care what you do. You're all on your own.

16
00:00:40,604 --> 00:00:42,304
As of today, I, Han Gyu Rim, resign from my role...

17
00:00:42,904 --> 00:00:43,904
as the eldest daughter of this house.

18
00:00:46,074 --> 00:00:47,074
Gyeol.

19
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:54,514
- Should we get sweet and sour pork? - Yes.

20
00:00:54,584 --> 00:00:55,584
Resign?

21
00:00:59,824 --> 00:01:02,094
My goodness, this is delicious, right?

22
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:05,394
- Sweet and sour pork's good too. - Was that you?

23
00:01:05,694 --> 00:01:06,694
Are you kidding me?

24
00:01:07,564 --> 00:01:10,494
- Darn it. - Only you would pick a fight here.

25
00:01:10,694 --> 00:01:14,164
- Father must've been the one. - What?

26
00:01:21,214 --> 00:01:23,114
- Mom. - Yes?

27
00:01:23,174 --> 00:01:24,544
I feel uncomfortable.

28
00:01:26,684 --> 00:01:29,754
It's okay. Just pretend no one else is here.

29
00:01:29,884 --> 00:01:31,124
Just ignore them and eat.

30
00:01:31,354 --> 00:01:33,824
Eating jajangmyeon after so long, it tastes so good, right?

31
00:01:34,154 --> 00:01:35,154
Yes.

32
00:01:39,524 --> 00:01:41,694
Darn it, who was it?

33
00:01:42,194 --> 00:01:44,394
Who pissed off the eldest daughter of this house?

34
00:01:45,464 --> 00:01:47,134
It's your fault.

35
00:01:47,404 --> 00:01:49,604
You're all grown up. Why the heck are you fighting?

36
00:01:50,174 --> 00:01:51,244
You're not kids anymore.

37
00:01:52,144 --> 00:01:53,344
I mean, fighting to the point where...

38
00:01:53,404 --> 00:01:54,744
you get dragged to the police station,

39
00:01:54,814 --> 00:01:55,944
are you in your right minds?

40
00:01:56,944 --> 00:01:59,144
I don't think you're in a position to say that, Father.

41
00:01:59,384 --> 00:02:01,814
- Exactly. - I was the victim.

42
00:02:02,214 --> 00:02:03,454
Some woman...

43
00:02:04,084 --> 00:02:06,084
dined and dashed, so I just left. That's all.

44
00:02:06,924 --> 00:02:07,994
You're seeing women again?

45
00:02:08,494 --> 00:02:10,294
I don't think you're one to talk.

46
00:02:11,794 --> 00:02:13,164
She was a woman, but...

47
00:02:13,764 --> 00:02:17,364
not that kind of woman. She just said she'd buy me tuna,

48
00:02:17,434 --> 00:02:18,804
so I went along with her.

49
00:02:19,434 --> 00:02:21,734
When is that man ever going to grow up? Seriously.

50
00:02:22,404 --> 00:02:23,404
"Man?"

51
00:02:24,034 --> 00:02:26,674
Hey, one day you're treating me like dirt,

52
00:02:26,844 --> 00:02:28,474
and now you're calling me "man" to my face?

53
00:02:28,914 --> 00:02:30,574
If you keep pushing my buttons like that,

54
00:02:30,644 --> 00:02:33,044
I just might crash your wedding.

55
00:02:33,284 --> 00:02:35,854
I'll wear a name tag that says "Han Gyu Young's real father"...

56
00:02:35,954 --> 00:02:38,554
and sit right there at the parents' table.

57
00:02:39,254 --> 00:02:41,394
Han Gyu Rim, you deal with Father.

58
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,094
Make sure he doesn't come anywhere near my wedding.

59
00:02:46,194 --> 00:02:48,864
Gyeol, I'm sorry, but for a while, when we're at home,

60
00:02:48,934 --> 00:02:50,664
how about we wear earphones?

61
00:02:51,164 --> 00:02:52,164
Why?

62
00:02:52,434 --> 00:02:53,834
The things everyone in this family says...

63
00:02:54,434 --> 00:02:56,274
are bad for your education.

64
00:03:03,714 --> 00:03:06,044
It's okay, Mom. I just tune them out.

65
00:03:08,184 --> 00:03:10,284
- Are you all done? - Yes.

66
00:03:10,384 --> 00:03:12,054
Go brush your teeth and do your homework now.

67
00:03:12,654 --> 00:03:13,654
Up you go.

68
00:03:15,754 --> 00:03:16,754
Okay.

69
00:03:19,424 --> 00:03:20,694
Thank you for the meal.

70
00:03:21,294 --> 00:03:22,294
Sure.

71
00:03:25,434 --> 00:03:26,634
I have something to say.

72
00:03:27,534 --> 00:03:28,974
Don't.

73
00:03:30,004 --> 00:03:31,404
You're acting weird today.

74
00:03:31,974 --> 00:03:33,274
Really weird.

75
00:03:33,644 --> 00:03:34,814
When you're acting this weird,

76
00:03:35,014 --> 00:03:36,744
it's best not to say anything.

77
00:03:37,014 --> 00:03:39,444
- I don't want to hear it. - Our house.

78
00:03:40,014 --> 00:03:41,454
We have to be out in three months.

79
00:03:42,754 --> 00:03:44,014
What are you talking about now?

80
00:03:44,354 --> 00:03:45,584
The landlord wants us to move out.

81
00:03:45,854 --> 00:03:47,224
We've had a good run living here so cheaply.

82
00:03:47,424 --> 00:03:48,954
Don't they just want to raise the rent?

83
00:03:49,794 --> 00:03:52,324
No, they just want us out. Period.

84
00:03:53,194 --> 00:03:54,664
Then where are we going to live?

85
00:03:55,494 --> 00:03:57,094
We'll each have to figure that out for ourselves.

86
00:03:59,504 --> 00:04:01,634
What do you mean, "figure that out for ourselves?"

87
00:04:01,974 --> 00:04:05,544
You find us a place. I'm fine as long as it's in Seoul.

88
00:04:08,374 --> 00:04:10,044
Why do I have to do everything?

89
00:04:12,214 --> 00:04:15,054
Because you're this family's eldest daughter.

90
00:04:15,114 --> 00:04:19,084
I told you earlier. I'm resigning as eldest daughter.

91
00:04:20,054 --> 00:04:21,294
Is "eldest daughter" a title you can resign from?

92
00:04:21,424 --> 00:04:23,154
Do you think you can just quit whenever you feel like it?

93
00:04:23,254 --> 00:04:25,494
The one who wants to be disowned should keep her mouth shut.

94
00:04:26,294 --> 00:04:28,194
What? Is something really going on with you?

95
00:04:28,364 --> 00:04:30,294
With the money we have now,

96
00:04:30,634 --> 00:04:32,104
our family can't live together anyway.

97
00:04:32,834 --> 00:04:34,134
Gyu Min and Gyu Seo...

98
00:04:35,334 --> 00:04:36,874
are minors, so until they become adults,

99
00:04:36,934 --> 00:04:38,974
they'll live with me and Gyeol.

100
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:42,114
Gyu Oh and Father should find your own places.

101
00:04:43,374 --> 00:04:44,414
I'm not...

102
00:04:45,014 --> 00:04:46,014
taking questions.

103
00:04:49,484 --> 00:04:52,724
So the twins, Gyeol, and you are going to live together,

104
00:04:52,784 --> 00:04:54,484
and I'm supposed to live with Gyu Oh?

105
00:04:54,554 --> 00:04:56,254
I'm not living with you, Father.

106
00:04:57,494 --> 00:04:59,764
Hey, Gyu Oh says he won't live with me.

107
00:04:59,824 --> 00:05:00,824
Then what am I supposed to do?

108
00:05:01,194 --> 00:05:02,934
You're dropping a lot of bombshells today.

109
00:05:03,164 --> 00:05:04,594
Have you been taking lessons or something?

110
00:05:04,704 --> 00:05:07,134
- Did you get lessons from someone? - Hey, Han Gyu Young.

111
00:05:07,204 --> 00:05:08,774
She said she's not taking questions.

112
00:05:08,874 --> 00:05:10,374
Han Gyu Rim isn't in her right mind.

113
00:05:10,434 --> 00:05:13,044
If we just let her be, I'll be the one stuck with all the crap.

114
00:05:14,944 --> 00:05:16,874
- Get out of my way. - Hey.

115
00:05:16,944 --> 00:05:18,244
- Hey. - Hey.

116
00:05:18,244 --> 00:05:19,644
- Hey. - What?

117
00:05:19,714 --> 00:05:20,714
Crap?

118
00:05:20,784 --> 00:05:22,684
Hey, is this family just crap to you?

119
00:05:22,754 --> 00:05:24,184
Well, are we a pot of gold?

120
00:05:24,514 --> 00:05:26,224
Hey, stop it, Han Gyu Young. Seriously.

121
00:05:26,284 --> 00:05:28,894
You stop her, Han Gyu Oh. Han Gyu Rim is so pigheaded.

122
00:05:29,054 --> 00:05:31,894
Once she really gets going, no one can stop her.

123
00:05:32,264 --> 00:05:34,964
Then you all should've stopped her from getting going.

124
00:05:35,034 --> 00:05:37,494
Why provoke her when she was being perfectly quiet...

125
00:05:37,564 --> 00:05:38,834
and cause all this trouble?

126
00:05:38,964 --> 00:05:41,304
Father, why don't you try to get your life together?

127
00:05:41,404 --> 00:05:42,734
What right do you have to eat fresh tuna?

128
00:05:42,804 --> 00:05:44,574
You can just eat canned tuna, you know.

129
00:05:45,144 --> 00:05:48,174
Did you pay for the tuna? Gyu Rim paid for it.

130
00:05:48,444 --> 00:05:50,874
You've never bought these kids so much as a piece of gum.

131
00:05:50,944 --> 00:05:52,544
Who are you to lecture me?

132
00:06:11,804 --> 00:06:13,904
So you really only did laundry for yourself and Gyeol.

133
00:06:15,904 --> 00:06:17,774
Fine, I get it.

134
00:06:17,974 --> 00:06:19,174
After dealing with Father, Gyu Oh, and Gyu Seo...

135
00:06:19,244 --> 00:06:20,944
and constantly bailing them out of the police station,

136
00:06:21,304 --> 00:06:23,644
you can get overloaded and break down.

137
00:06:24,244 --> 00:06:26,344
You're only human. You can get exhausted.

138
00:06:26,414 --> 00:06:27,684
You think, "Why is my life like this?"

139
00:06:27,744 --> 00:06:28,884
Your self-esteem hits rock bottom,

140
00:06:29,154 --> 00:06:30,614
and it's natural to feel jaded and think,

141
00:06:30,684 --> 00:06:32,054
"What's the point of living like this?"

142
00:06:32,554 --> 00:06:35,824
I completely understand how much you've suffered,

143
00:06:35,894 --> 00:06:39,024
and there have been times I've felt sorry for you too.

144
00:06:40,524 --> 00:06:42,594
So just hang in there a little longer.

145
00:06:42,964 --> 00:06:44,764
Once I get married and get my inheritance,

146
00:06:44,964 --> 00:06:48,004
I'll make sure to fully repay you for everything you've been through.

147
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:49,074
Get...

148
00:06:50,404 --> 00:06:51,404
lost.

149
00:06:51,674 --> 00:06:52,674
What?

150
00:06:52,904 --> 00:06:54,944
"Get lost?" What? You're telling me to get lost?

151
00:06:57,444 --> 00:06:58,714
I'm practising my English conversation.

152
00:06:59,914 --> 00:07:03,114
That's ridiculous. You? Practising English?

153
00:07:03,184 --> 00:07:05,284
They say the most important thing in conversation is confidence.

154
00:07:05,624 --> 00:07:07,454
Don't worry about making mistakes or hesitate.

155
00:07:07,524 --> 00:07:10,094
They say you should just say it with confidence.

156
00:07:10,354 --> 00:07:11,694
Get lost.

157
00:07:12,524 --> 00:07:14,964
You're not some rebellious teenager. Seriously, what are you doing?

158
00:07:15,364 --> 00:07:16,894
You know what they say. When people change, they die.

159
00:07:16,964 --> 00:07:17,964
Exactly.

160
00:07:18,334 --> 00:07:19,804
The Han Gyu Rim you used to know is dead.

161
00:07:21,504 --> 00:07:24,234
Can you speak slowly?

162
00:07:24,504 --> 00:07:27,104
What is that?

163
00:07:27,744 --> 00:07:29,314
Has she really lost her mind?

164
00:07:29,644 --> 00:07:31,544
Get lost?

165
00:07:32,114 --> 00:07:33,284
That's ridiculous.

166
00:07:42,824 --> 00:07:43,994
Are you making sandwiches?

167
00:07:44,754 --> 00:07:45,764
Yes.

168
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,124
Gyeol asked me to make them.

169
00:07:49,164 --> 00:07:50,194
Do you want one too?

170
00:07:50,894 --> 00:07:53,534
No. I thought you said we're all fending for ourselves now.

171
00:07:53,664 --> 00:07:55,134
I'll make my own food.

172
00:07:55,834 --> 00:07:57,504
Gyu Seo said he'll get his own food too.

173
00:07:57,934 --> 00:07:59,144
Don't worry about us.

174
00:07:59,974 --> 00:08:02,544
- Okay, let's do that. - Yes.

175
00:08:03,574 --> 00:08:04,744
You did the right thing.

176
00:08:04,944 --> 00:08:06,744
You should have done this a long time ago.

177
00:08:10,054 --> 00:08:11,454
Gyeol is going to love these.

178
00:08:13,824 --> 00:08:15,394
Oh, I was watching TV,

179
00:08:15,624 --> 00:08:18,264
and they said warty sea squirts are in season.

180
00:08:20,694 --> 00:08:21,694
Gyu Rim.

181
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,494
Should we make some soybean paste stew...

182
00:08:23,564 --> 00:08:24,834
with warty sea squirt?

183
00:08:25,804 --> 00:08:26,864
Make it yourself.

184
00:08:28,404 --> 00:08:30,404
The soybean paste and vegetables are in the fridge,

185
00:08:30,474 --> 00:08:32,544
and they should sell warty sea squirts at the supermarket.

186
00:08:35,974 --> 00:08:37,744
I get it if the kids act this way,

187
00:08:39,284 --> 00:08:41,084
but shouldn't you make an exception for me?

188
00:08:42,484 --> 00:08:44,854
I'm your father. You're supposed to take care of me.

189
00:08:46,024 --> 00:08:48,254
Then would you like a sandwich, Father?

190
00:08:48,794 --> 00:08:51,124
I don't eat bread in the morning.

191
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:54,594
Just make me soybean paste stew with warty sea squirt.

192
00:08:55,334 --> 00:08:56,994
I don't want to make soybean paste stew.

193
00:08:57,364 --> 00:08:59,904
And I don't like warty sea squirt.

194
00:09:04,474 --> 00:09:06,804
Han Gyeol, are you all ready for school?

195
00:09:10,114 --> 00:09:11,744
Let's eat the sandwiches.

196
00:09:17,984 --> 00:09:21,994
Hey, is that really your sister, Han Gyu Rim?

197
00:09:22,624 --> 00:09:23,924
This is incredible.

198
00:09:24,154 --> 00:09:26,894
My sister has suddenly gotten so cool.

199
00:09:26,964 --> 00:09:29,964
- What's with you now? - What?

200
00:10:15,814 --> 00:10:17,344
Hey, what is all this?

201
00:10:17,414 --> 00:10:18,784
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

202
00:10:19,184 --> 00:10:21,784
I went to the fish market and they had some really good croaker.

203
00:10:21,854 --> 00:10:23,184
Oh my.

204
00:10:23,584 --> 00:10:25,854
But what should I do? Seo Hyun left early in the morning.

205
00:10:25,924 --> 00:10:27,024
She said she had to prepare for a meeting.

206
00:10:27,084 --> 00:10:29,324
I brought this for you and Ma'am.

207
00:10:30,694 --> 00:10:33,224
- Oh my. - But is she not home?

208
00:10:33,294 --> 00:10:35,564
She went out to buy some dried pollack...

209
00:10:35,634 --> 00:10:39,534
- to make me hangover soup. - I heard she likes croaker.

210
00:10:39,864 --> 00:10:41,134
I'll slice this for sashimi right away,

211
00:10:41,204 --> 00:10:43,174
and I'll make a stew and some pancakes for you too.

212
00:10:44,034 --> 00:10:45,244
All right.

213
00:10:45,774 --> 00:10:46,904
Hey, Mu Jin.

214
00:10:47,374 --> 00:10:49,614
You know, this bold approach of yours,

215
00:10:49,674 --> 00:10:51,074
I'm really all for it.

216
00:10:51,914 --> 00:10:53,144
But I don't know.

217
00:10:53,214 --> 00:10:56,414
I'm not sure if Yoon Hee will be as moved...

218
00:10:56,714 --> 00:10:57,984
Oh, that's all right.

219
00:10:58,054 --> 00:11:01,424
As long as you enjoy the meal, I'll be happy.

220
00:11:01,484 --> 00:11:05,464
All right. You're the bigger man. Anything I can do to help?

221
00:11:05,524 --> 00:11:07,494
No, I brought my own knife and cutting board,

222
00:11:07,564 --> 00:11:08,894
so please don't worry about me.

223
00:11:09,034 --> 00:11:11,064
- You can just sit and relax. - You think so?

224
00:11:12,934 --> 00:11:14,334
I think Yoon Hee is back.

225
00:11:14,834 --> 00:11:17,304
- I'm in here. - Yes, I'm back.

226
00:11:17,374 --> 00:11:18,374
Yes.

227
00:11:21,204 --> 00:11:22,314
Hello.

228
00:11:24,944 --> 00:11:26,444
Mu Jin...

229
00:11:26,584 --> 00:11:28,854
heard you like croaker, so he brought some.

230
00:11:28,914 --> 00:11:30,714
And today, our Chef here...

231
00:11:30,884 --> 00:11:32,884
is going to cook everything for us. Right?

232
00:11:34,154 --> 00:11:35,624
You think I'm a joke, don't you?

233
00:11:37,254 --> 00:11:38,394
Honey.

234
00:11:38,694 --> 00:11:40,324
Is this the "effort" you promised to make?

235
00:11:41,624 --> 00:11:42,994
To be this rude...

236
00:11:43,534 --> 00:11:45,264
and make me feel this uncomfortable?

237
00:11:47,764 --> 00:11:50,304
How can you call this effort when it's so aggressive and selfish?

238
00:11:50,404 --> 00:11:51,404
Honey.

239
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:55,914
I apologise if I've made you uncomfortable.

240
00:11:56,774 --> 00:11:58,914
If you're really sorry, then don't ever do this again.

241
00:12:07,084 --> 00:12:08,854
Oh, man. I'm so sorry about this.

242
00:12:10,594 --> 00:12:13,094
It's all right. I guess I wasn't thinking straight.

243
00:12:14,664 --> 00:12:18,164
I'll leave the croaker here. Ma'am is an excellent cook,

244
00:12:18,264 --> 00:12:19,404
so I hope you enjoy it.

245
00:12:20,104 --> 00:12:21,874
- Mu Jin. - Yes.

246
00:12:22,134 --> 00:12:24,504
You're not going to stop visiting us now, are you?

247
00:12:24,704 --> 00:12:25,904
Of course not.

248
00:12:26,044 --> 00:12:27,204
I'll be back soon.

249
00:12:27,474 --> 00:12:30,474
When I do, please just open the door for me like you did today.

250
00:12:31,044 --> 00:12:33,584
All right. Thanks for the croaker.

251
00:13:05,544 --> 00:13:06,914
Mu Jin left.

252
00:13:09,584 --> 00:13:10,584
Honey.

253
00:13:11,484 --> 00:13:12,984
You know, I think...

254
00:13:13,324 --> 00:13:15,654
that your being so against him like this...

255
00:13:16,294 --> 00:13:18,054
means there's more to it than how Mu Jin...

256
00:13:18,124 --> 00:13:19,824
broke our Seo Hyun's heart.

257
00:13:20,494 --> 00:13:23,234
There has to be another serious reason.

258
00:13:26,004 --> 00:13:27,834
Can't you tell me what that is?

259
00:13:30,534 --> 00:13:34,974
Did you hear a rumour or something? For example, that Mu Jin...

260
00:13:35,044 --> 00:13:37,774
has some terrible disease or something like that.

261
00:13:39,314 --> 00:13:40,814
I'll go prepare our meal.

262
00:13:41,444 --> 00:13:42,454
Honey.

263
00:13:43,384 --> 00:13:45,254
What? Does he have a gambling problem?

264
00:13:46,454 --> 00:13:48,184
Or is he a notorious womanizer?

265
00:13:48,324 --> 00:13:50,554
Like he has more than 1 or 2 women on the side,

266
00:13:50,624 --> 00:13:53,194
- is it something like that? - It's nothing like that.

267
00:13:54,164 --> 00:13:55,164
Come on, you have to give me something...

268
00:13:55,234 --> 00:13:57,834
I can understand so I can be on your side.

269
00:14:02,334 --> 00:14:04,104
I'm sorry. It's because of me.

270
00:14:06,244 --> 00:14:08,104
That's not what I'm trying to hear...

271
00:14:08,404 --> 00:14:09,474
I'm...

272
00:14:10,074 --> 00:14:12,884
just saying that I want to understand you.

273
00:14:18,484 --> 00:14:20,484
You would never understand.

274
00:14:30,234 --> 00:14:32,634
Hey, get out of the way, you fool.

275
00:14:32,704 --> 00:14:35,834
Hey, will you move, you fool. Get out of my way now, you jerk.

276
00:14:36,204 --> 00:14:38,434
I'm telling you to write a promise, aren't I?

277
00:14:39,844 --> 00:14:41,044
That you won't pick on Gyu Rim ever again.

278
00:14:41,104 --> 00:14:42,514
I'm telling you to write it down.

279
00:14:43,474 --> 00:14:45,344
Pick on her? How did I pick on her?

280
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:48,144
Gyeol's Mom, that little thing, just went to you...

281
00:14:48,214 --> 00:14:50,654
and tattled on me, didn't she?

282
00:14:50,714 --> 00:14:53,224
Gyu Rim didn't tattle. Okay?

283
00:14:53,524 --> 00:14:55,154
You've been mistreating her...

284
00:14:55,224 --> 00:14:58,294
and making her do all the hard work, and you're trying to kick her out.

285
00:14:58,354 --> 00:14:59,924
The rumour is all over the market.

286
00:15:00,824 --> 00:15:04,264
Oh, please. I'm not even close to being done, you hear?

287
00:15:04,664 --> 00:15:06,364
The vixen who toyed with my precious son...

288
00:15:06,434 --> 00:15:10,174
you think this is all she deserves? This is just the beginning.

289
00:15:10,604 --> 00:15:12,844
I'm not even a tenth of the way done.

290
00:15:12,904 --> 00:15:14,974
She didn't dump me, I dumped her.

291
00:15:15,044 --> 00:15:17,574
How many times do I have to say it?

292
00:15:18,444 --> 00:15:22,414
And you expect me to believe that?

293
00:15:23,054 --> 00:15:24,254
If I let my anger get the best of me,

294
00:15:24,314 --> 00:15:25,724
even ripping out all her hair...

295
00:15:25,784 --> 00:15:27,654
wouldn't be satisfying enough. Darn it.

296
00:15:30,094 --> 00:15:33,564
Just try and lay a finger on Gyu Rim.

297
00:15:33,664 --> 00:15:35,334
For every hair on her head you touch,

298
00:15:35,394 --> 00:15:36,934
I'll get ten degrees more twisted.

299
00:15:37,594 --> 00:15:39,304
And you know what happens when I get twisted, don't you?

300
00:15:39,364 --> 00:15:41,804
Goodness, you spineless fool.

301
00:15:41,864 --> 00:15:44,404
Goodness, you've lost your mind.

302
00:15:44,804 --> 00:15:46,974
Give me back the phone you took and get out of my way, you punk.

303
00:15:47,044 --> 00:15:48,044
Why?

304
00:15:48,104 --> 00:15:49,114
What will you do if I return the phone?

305
00:15:49,174 --> 00:15:50,274
Call Gyu Rim and curse her out?

306
00:15:50,344 --> 00:15:52,744
- That's right. - Until you write that promise,

307
00:15:52,814 --> 00:15:55,314
you're not getting your phone back, and I'm not moving.

308
00:16:00,324 --> 00:16:01,884
Okay, where are you? Are you almost here?

309
00:16:02,494 --> 00:16:03,824
Yes, I'm right outside.

310
00:16:03,994 --> 00:16:06,364
Let go of me, you punk. You rotten brat.

311
00:16:06,424 --> 00:16:08,464
- Sit down, will you? - Let go.

312
00:16:09,934 --> 00:16:10,934
I'm here.

313
00:16:11,834 --> 00:16:14,064
I figured you were the only one free at this hour,

314
00:16:14,434 --> 00:16:16,504
so just watch this old lady for me for now. Okay?

315
00:16:17,104 --> 00:16:18,104
Why?

316
00:16:18,334 --> 00:16:20,504
He's worried I'm going to go bother Han Gyu Rim,

317
00:16:20,674 --> 00:16:24,174
so that rotten punk won't let me move an inch.

318
00:16:24,374 --> 00:16:26,684
Wait, Ma'am, why are you mistreating my sister?

319
00:16:26,744 --> 00:16:28,714
Hey, ask your questions when you two are alone.

320
00:16:28,784 --> 00:16:31,454
For now, just don't let her leave. If she gets out,

321
00:16:31,514 --> 00:16:32,724
your sister is in big trouble. Got it?

322
00:16:33,084 --> 00:16:34,284
Until she writes the promise,

323
00:16:34,354 --> 00:16:37,494
- make sure she doesn't leave. - Yes.

324
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:43,564
Hey, give me back my phone. I hope you fall flat on your face.

325
00:16:43,694 --> 00:16:46,364
That rotten punk. Oh, I'm exhausted.

326
00:16:46,434 --> 00:16:49,434
(Suragan Side Dishes)

327
00:16:54,004 --> 00:16:56,114
Man, this old lady. Seriously.

328
00:16:56,214 --> 00:16:57,874
(Now Hiring, Honest Person Preferred)

329
00:17:02,254 --> 00:17:04,884
- Welcome, Heung Sik. - Gyu Rim.

330
00:17:06,724 --> 00:17:08,424
Is your mother feeling any better?

331
00:17:08,584 --> 00:17:10,024
Her phone was turned off.

332
00:17:10,324 --> 00:17:13,524
Oh, she turned it off to sleep. It's just a small stomachache.

333
00:17:13,594 --> 00:17:15,864
She said she'll be fine after some medicine and a good rest.

334
00:17:17,194 --> 00:17:19,434
She's not sick because of me, is she?

335
00:17:19,734 --> 00:17:21,664
No. My mom is the type of person...

336
00:17:21,734 --> 00:17:24,004
who gets more energized the angrier she is.

337
00:17:24,704 --> 00:17:26,774
But why aren't you with your mother?

338
00:17:26,844 --> 00:17:27,904
Why did you come here?

339
00:17:28,444 --> 00:17:29,444
Well...

340
00:17:29,914 --> 00:17:32,114
My grandmother told me to come help you...

341
00:17:32,184 --> 00:17:33,944
in her place.

342
00:17:34,044 --> 00:17:37,114
Look at this. This is too much for you to do alone.

343
00:17:37,654 --> 00:17:39,554
No, it's okay. I can do it by myself...

344
00:17:42,494 --> 00:17:45,394
Really? Actually, we have a lot of delivery orders today,

345
00:17:45,464 --> 00:17:46,624
so I could use the help.

346
00:17:46,694 --> 00:17:49,834
See? I knew it. I'll do anything,

347
00:17:50,164 --> 00:17:52,664
so just order me around as much as you want. Okay?

348
00:17:58,744 --> 00:17:59,744
Honestly.

349
00:18:01,904 --> 00:18:04,614
Today's deliveries are for...

350
00:18:05,144 --> 00:18:08,444
- Dajeong complex three... - That's weird.

351
00:18:08,714 --> 00:18:10,854
- Why? What is it? - Hey.

352
00:18:11,214 --> 00:18:14,824
Stare at me like you're trying to burn a hole through my eyes.

353
00:18:16,794 --> 00:18:17,794
Like this?

354
00:18:21,864 --> 00:18:22,864
I'm okay.

355
00:18:23,864 --> 00:18:25,504
I'm not even that nervous anymore,

356
00:18:25,964 --> 00:18:27,564
and I'm much better than I was yesterday.

357
00:18:28,134 --> 00:18:29,134
If this keeps up,

358
00:18:29,134 --> 00:18:30,734
I'll be able to look at you as if you were a stone.

359
00:18:32,504 --> 00:18:34,444
Should I keep looking at you like this?

360
00:18:34,744 --> 00:18:37,414
No, no. You can get back to work now. Go on.

361
00:18:39,644 --> 00:18:42,614
Whatever the boss says to me, please stay out of it.

362
00:18:43,154 --> 00:18:46,024
Please let me be the one to solve this.

363
00:18:46,184 --> 00:18:47,184
That's how you can help me.

364
00:18:47,954 --> 00:18:50,594
Of course. I won't do a thing.

365
00:18:50,954 --> 00:18:52,624
It looks like you already did something.

366
00:18:53,294 --> 00:18:55,964
You didn't lock the boss in her house, did you?

367
00:18:56,164 --> 00:18:57,294
So she couldn't give me a hard time.

368
00:18:57,564 --> 00:19:02,434
No. I would never. Now, get to work.

369
00:19:03,474 --> 00:19:05,374
- Darn it... - Something's off.

370
00:19:08,374 --> 00:19:10,444
Why can't I understand you?

371
00:19:12,144 --> 00:19:14,784
Why do you think I can never understand you?

372
00:19:18,384 --> 00:19:20,624
What am I missing?

373
00:19:30,694 --> 00:19:31,694
Chairman Jang.

374
00:19:33,804 --> 00:19:34,804
Jang Hoon Tae.

375
00:19:43,844 --> 00:19:44,974
Looks like the meeting with the chancellor...

376
00:19:45,044 --> 00:19:47,114
is running a bit long. He said he'll be here soon.

377
00:19:48,614 --> 00:19:50,914
Hey, I didn't realise Professor Cha invited you too.

378
00:19:51,954 --> 00:19:53,554
Cha Yeong Su and I are closer, you know.

379
00:19:53,684 --> 00:19:54,854
I know you're close.

380
00:19:56,054 --> 00:19:57,454
Hey, if we're talking about being close,

381
00:19:57,524 --> 00:19:59,394
Cha Yeong Su and I went to elementary school together.

382
00:20:00,094 --> 00:20:01,564
We went to kindergarten together.

383
00:20:02,694 --> 00:20:04,734
Really? I had no idea.

384
00:20:09,434 --> 00:20:10,434
Hey.

385
00:20:11,434 --> 00:20:13,674
Did you tell Cha Yeong Su about our kids?

386
00:20:14,674 --> 00:20:15,874
Are you crazy?

387
00:20:15,974 --> 00:20:18,114
Right? Then why did he invite us both?

388
00:20:18,274 --> 00:20:19,344
My gosh.

389
00:20:20,714 --> 00:20:23,884
Gosh, I was hoping not to see you for a while.

390
00:20:26,484 --> 00:20:29,354
Seriously, what is with your wife?

391
00:20:29,794 --> 00:20:31,824
How dare she mistreat my precious son...

392
00:20:31,894 --> 00:20:33,194
and turn him away like that?

393
00:20:33,594 --> 00:20:35,294
If she keeps testing my patience like this,

394
00:20:35,364 --> 00:20:37,164
I'm not going to just stand by. I'm serious.

395
00:20:37,564 --> 00:20:38,694
So what do you want me to do?

396
00:20:39,664 --> 00:20:41,004
What, should I get on my knees?

397
00:20:43,804 --> 00:20:45,604
You say that like you'd actually do it if I asked.

398
00:20:47,144 --> 00:20:51,374
- If you tell me to, I will. - Then do it. Get on your knees.

399
00:20:52,844 --> 00:20:55,584
Hey, hey. Get up.

400
00:20:56,414 --> 00:20:57,414
Get up.

401
00:20:58,314 --> 00:20:59,554
Hey, why are you kneeling?

402
00:20:59,624 --> 00:21:01,254
If anyone's going to kneel, it should be your wife.

403
00:21:01,324 --> 00:21:02,494
I don't have a problem with you.

404
00:21:02,554 --> 00:21:03,924
It's your wife I have a problem with.

405
00:21:04,094 --> 00:21:06,024
Hey, that's the problem, don't you see?

406
00:21:06,464 --> 00:21:08,094
A husband and wife are one and the same.

407
00:21:08,164 --> 00:21:11,634
I am my wife, and my wife is me. So just put up with it for my sake.

408
00:21:12,164 --> 00:21:13,904
Oh, for crying out loud.

409
00:21:14,034 --> 00:21:16,434
How is a woman without a husband supposed to put up with this?

410
00:21:18,234 --> 00:21:19,244
Just hang in there a little longer.

411
00:21:22,274 --> 00:21:23,844
That punk Yeong Su invited two busy chairmen here...

412
00:21:23,914 --> 00:21:25,984
then went off somewhere and still hasn't come back...

413
00:21:26,344 --> 00:21:29,284
- I'm leaving. - Hey, calm down. Be patient.

414
00:21:29,354 --> 00:21:30,654
You won't age gracefully if you act like that.

415
00:21:30,984 --> 00:21:32,654
I am already ageing gracefully, thank you.

416
00:21:32,784 --> 00:21:33,854
Yes?

417
00:21:34,254 --> 00:21:38,224
Hey, some people say I look ten years younger than I am.

418
00:21:39,994 --> 00:21:43,164
Really? Wow, that's some line.

419
00:21:44,364 --> 00:21:45,364
It was a man, wasn't it?

420
00:21:46,434 --> 00:21:47,634
Well, it wasn't a woman.

421
00:21:47,704 --> 00:21:48,834
Right.

422
00:21:50,004 --> 00:21:51,374
Watch out for scammers, too.

423
00:21:52,744 --> 00:21:54,204
Then again, our Chairman Hong...

424
00:21:54,274 --> 00:21:57,444
is smart enough to spot a scammer who's only after her money. Right?

425
00:21:58,444 --> 00:22:00,444
- Please, eat up. - Yes.

426
00:22:05,754 --> 00:22:06,754
Yes?

427
00:22:07,224 --> 00:22:10,054
Oh, please go ahead and eat. I have to take this call.

428
00:22:10,124 --> 00:22:12,124
- Oh, yes. Of course. - Hello?

429
00:22:16,334 --> 00:22:17,564
I'm the one who scammed him.

430
00:22:20,664 --> 00:22:23,134
I said I'd treat him to tuna.

431
00:22:24,374 --> 00:22:26,144
What's wrong with me these days, Hoon Tae?

432
00:22:26,974 --> 00:22:29,244
I think I'm getting dementia. What am I going to do?

433
00:22:29,844 --> 00:22:31,144
What are you talking about? Tuna?

434
00:22:44,454 --> 00:22:45,794
Do you know of any cults?

435
00:22:46,394 --> 00:22:47,794
Or any sham religions you know of?

436
00:22:48,794 --> 00:22:49,794
It's just that my Gyu Rim...

437
00:22:49,864 --> 00:22:51,294
has been acting strange all of a sudden.

438
00:22:52,164 --> 00:22:55,904
You know how in those documentaries, they say when people join a cult,

439
00:22:55,974 --> 00:22:58,174
they're told to cut off their families first?

440
00:22:59,804 --> 00:23:01,344
My eldest daughter...

441
00:23:04,644 --> 00:23:07,014
She's the type who would do anything for her family.

442
00:23:08,314 --> 00:23:11,384
Anyway, I'm thinking of having her followed first.

443
00:23:12,454 --> 00:23:13,454
Okay, got it.

444
00:23:13,754 --> 00:23:16,324
I'll call you again when I have more details.

445
00:23:16,594 --> 00:23:17,594
Okay.

446
00:23:18,024 --> 00:23:22,564
Sir, I am so sorry. Something urgent came up,

447
00:23:22,764 --> 00:23:26,564
and I completely forgot you were in the private room eating tuna.

448
00:23:28,334 --> 00:23:29,374
It's all right.

449
00:23:30,234 --> 00:23:34,374
- I guess I'm just that unmemorable. - It's not you, it's me.

450
00:23:34,444 --> 00:23:37,274
My memory has been getting so bad lately...

451
00:23:37,514 --> 00:23:39,644
I know someone who blames their bad memory...

452
00:23:39,714 --> 00:23:41,244
when they have nothing to say.

453
00:23:41,944 --> 00:23:42,954
Look...

454
00:23:44,884 --> 00:23:47,584
I'll pay for the bill from last time.

455
00:23:48,224 --> 00:23:51,554
And as an apology, I'd like to treat you to tuna again.

456
00:23:52,664 --> 00:23:56,164
Forget it. Now, just hearing the word "tuna" makes me sick.

457
00:23:58,794 --> 00:24:00,464
- Excuse me, would you like... - Give us a minute.

458
00:24:05,104 --> 00:24:08,174
Then I'll treat you to something even better than tuna.

459
00:24:10,444 --> 00:24:12,584
What in the world is better than tuna?

460
00:24:14,244 --> 00:24:16,484
I think long tooth grouper is more delicious than tuna.

461
00:24:18,884 --> 00:24:20,224
You've had long tooth grouper before?

462
00:24:21,524 --> 00:24:22,954
It was probably an imitation.

463
00:24:23,024 --> 00:24:25,254
No, it was the real thing.

464
00:24:25,594 --> 00:24:27,024
Not a fake like seven-banded grouper.

465
00:24:27,724 --> 00:24:28,794
Did you use to own a seafood restaurant?

466
00:24:29,434 --> 00:24:30,464
You even know seven-banded grouper.

467
00:24:32,904 --> 00:24:34,864
You seem to know your stuff.

468
00:24:36,004 --> 00:24:38,034
Well, I ran one for a little while, a long time ago.

469
00:24:38,404 --> 00:24:40,874
Anyway, since I'm treating you to real long tooth grouper,

470
00:24:40,944 --> 00:24:42,744
please forget about the tuna.

471
00:24:44,914 --> 00:24:47,714
Do you have any idea how much long tooth grouper costs?

472
00:24:48,114 --> 00:24:50,084
They can charge whatever they want for it.

473
00:24:50,254 --> 00:24:52,054
I told you my savings club paid out.

474
00:24:54,654 --> 00:24:57,194
I promise I won't disappear this time.

475
00:24:57,294 --> 00:24:59,224
If you don't believe me, I can pay for it in advance.

476
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:02,294
Forget it. Just eat your noodles.

477
00:25:03,064 --> 00:25:04,134
Sir, please.

478
00:25:06,264 --> 00:25:07,564
If I were to eat long tooth grouper,

479
00:25:09,004 --> 00:25:10,534
I'm afraid I might start to cry.

480
00:25:12,204 --> 00:25:15,874
I'll remember my glory days...

481
00:25:16,714 --> 00:25:18,214
when tuna was everyday food to me...

482
00:25:18,974 --> 00:25:22,754
and the mistakes that ruined them.

483
00:25:30,754 --> 00:25:32,864
If you feel bad, you can buy me braised carp sometime.

484
00:25:44,004 --> 00:25:45,034
Go ahead and order.

485
00:25:48,304 --> 00:25:49,344
Yes, over here.

486
00:25:52,044 --> 00:25:54,544
Mu Jin came to our house?

487
00:25:57,054 --> 00:25:58,584
He brought this huge croaker,

488
00:25:58,654 --> 00:26:00,584
saying it was your mother's favourite,

489
00:26:01,854 --> 00:26:03,524
a massive one...

490
00:26:03,954 --> 00:26:06,324
and even brought all his own tools to cook it himself.

491
00:26:07,724 --> 00:26:08,724
But it was a total failure.

492
00:26:11,794 --> 00:26:12,804
This isn't working.

493
00:26:14,104 --> 00:26:16,574
I'm just going to register our marriage first.

494
00:26:16,934 --> 00:26:19,104
Register your marriage? By yourself?

495
00:26:20,144 --> 00:26:21,244
Do you think Mu Jin will agree to that?

496
00:26:24,214 --> 00:26:26,484
What is with my mom?

497
00:26:28,244 --> 00:26:30,154
I know. I thought she'd just be angry...

498
00:26:30,214 --> 00:26:31,584
for a bit and get over it.

499
00:26:32,184 --> 00:26:34,784
I don't get it either. She's usually so kind.

500
00:26:35,024 --> 00:26:37,594
So I've been thinking about why my mom is doing this,

501
00:26:37,594 --> 00:26:40,124
and I've considered every possible scenario, you know?

502
00:26:40,994 --> 00:26:45,064
But there is one thing I'm suspicious about.

503
00:26:46,734 --> 00:26:48,534
- Me too. - You too?

504
00:26:50,134 --> 00:26:51,134
What is it?

505
00:26:55,474 --> 00:26:56,514
You go first.

506
00:27:03,284 --> 00:27:06,154
My dad and Mu Jin's mom...

507
00:27:06,584 --> 00:27:08,824
weren't just friends. They used to date.

508
00:27:09,824 --> 00:27:12,054
And my mom must have just found out about it.

509
00:27:12,324 --> 00:27:14,764
Oh my, jinx.

510
00:27:15,624 --> 00:27:16,634
No way.

511
00:27:17,594 --> 00:27:18,594
Famous last words.

512
00:27:18,664 --> 00:27:20,664
We're both old enough to know better.

513
00:27:20,864 --> 00:27:22,934
Oh crap. Then what do we do?

514
00:27:24,774 --> 00:27:25,834
You'll have to break up.

515
00:27:26,104 --> 00:27:27,804
No way. Why should I?

516
00:27:30,944 --> 00:27:32,684
My theory goes even further.

517
00:27:36,354 --> 00:27:39,084
What if Mu Jin's father...

518
00:27:40,254 --> 00:27:41,684
is actually your father?

519
00:27:42,824 --> 00:27:43,824
Are you crazy?

520
00:27:43,894 --> 00:27:45,354
Hey, all due respect to Mu Jin's mother.

521
00:27:45,494 --> 00:27:46,764
The Chairman said so herself.

522
00:27:47,164 --> 00:27:49,934
That Mu Jin acts just like Chairman Jang.

523
00:27:50,034 --> 00:27:52,434
He's a spitting image of him, like a father and son.

524
00:27:52,494 --> 00:27:55,064
You're insane. You can't just say things like that.

525
00:27:55,234 --> 00:27:57,634
Who do you think you're joking about right now?

526
00:27:57,774 --> 00:28:00,404
What on earth do you take my father for?

527
00:28:00,474 --> 00:28:01,604
Are you in your right mind, Park Jung Woo?

528
00:28:04,274 --> 00:28:07,844
Don't let me see you again. Or I'll kill you.

529
00:28:16,194 --> 00:28:17,554
I really went too far.

530
00:28:19,524 --> 00:28:20,964
This stupid mouth of mine.

531
00:28:23,734 --> 00:28:26,804
Gosh, that hurts. She sure packs a punch.

532
00:28:30,934 --> 00:28:32,134
(Seo Hyun's Mother)

533
00:28:35,804 --> 00:28:36,844
Yes, Ma'am.

534
00:28:37,444 --> 00:28:39,384
I'm calling to ask a favour, Jung Woo.

535
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:41,944
This...

536
00:28:42,514 --> 00:28:44,784
has to be a secret between you and me.

537
00:28:46,624 --> 00:28:48,654
That girl who dated Mu Jin.

538
00:28:50,054 --> 00:28:51,594
Her name was Han Gyu Rim, right?

539
00:28:53,564 --> 00:28:54,564
Her.

540
00:28:55,324 --> 00:28:56,894
Where can I find her?

541
00:28:57,564 --> 00:29:00,364
Braised potatoes, young radish kimchi,

542
00:29:00,434 --> 00:29:01,964
and mung bean pancakes?

543
00:29:03,104 --> 00:29:05,534
Our spicy beef soup turned out really delicious this time.

544
00:29:05,604 --> 00:29:06,704
Would you like to try some?

545
00:29:08,844 --> 00:29:09,844
I mean, the seasoning this time...

546
00:29:09,914 --> 00:29:12,144
(Suragan Side Dishes)

547
00:29:15,584 --> 00:29:18,284
How about some braised soybeans on the house?

548
00:29:19,084 --> 00:29:20,124
Look at her go.

549
00:29:20,754 --> 00:29:22,654
Even with Grandma giving her a hard time,

550
00:29:22,724 --> 00:29:23,794
she's not fazed at all.

551
00:29:23,854 --> 00:29:25,454
Yes, thank you.

552
00:29:25,994 --> 00:29:30,264
- Okay, I'll add the soybeans then. - Since you insist,

553
00:29:30,334 --> 00:29:32,664
I'm not going to help you one bit anymore,

554
00:29:33,064 --> 00:29:35,264
so you're on your own from now on, Han Gyu Rim.

555
00:29:40,004 --> 00:29:41,174
(Gyu Oh)

556
00:29:41,944 --> 00:29:43,174
Oh, hey, Gyu Oh.

557
00:29:43,244 --> 00:29:44,714
I'm on my way back from a delivery now.

558
00:29:44,914 --> 00:29:46,284
Is Grandma doing okay?

559
00:29:48,014 --> 00:29:49,854
Right, it's really tough over there, isn't it?

560
00:29:50,214 --> 00:29:53,084
I'll be there soon. Oh, hang on. I have another call.

561
00:29:54,224 --> 00:29:56,224
Why is this brat calling me?

562
00:29:58,194 --> 00:29:59,194
Gyu Oh,

563
00:29:59,624 --> 00:30:01,624
Gyu Young's calling. I'll call you right back.

564
00:30:07,904 --> 00:30:09,474
Did you call me by mistake?

565
00:30:09,534 --> 00:30:12,474
Sir, are you busy?

566
00:30:12,974 --> 00:30:14,404
Are you sure you meant to call me?

567
00:30:15,104 --> 00:30:17,274
It's Heung Sik. Jo Heung Sik.

568
00:30:26,754 --> 00:30:27,824
Over here.

569
00:30:28,284 --> 00:30:29,724
Is she crazy?

570
00:30:34,294 --> 00:30:35,294
Surprise.

571
00:30:40,904 --> 00:30:43,234
I thought you might like something sweet,

572
00:30:43,304 --> 00:30:45,204
so I ordered you a vanilla latte.

573
00:30:47,004 --> 00:30:48,404
Are you sick?

574
00:30:49,344 --> 00:30:50,514
Have you checked your temperature?

575
00:30:51,744 --> 00:30:53,644
I know. It's weird seeing me like this, isn't it?

576
00:30:53,744 --> 00:30:56,784
But when I want something, I can be incredibly sweet.

577
00:30:57,984 --> 00:30:59,524
What is it that you want from me?

578
00:31:02,454 --> 00:31:04,654
You know who Park Bun Rye is, right?

579
00:31:05,154 --> 00:31:07,894
The name on my mother's ID.

580
00:31:08,194 --> 00:31:09,324
Exactly.

581
00:31:09,394 --> 00:31:11,364
That's what I found when I looked into it.

582
00:31:12,164 --> 00:31:13,164
And?

583
00:31:14,804 --> 00:31:17,934
The registry says Ms. Park Bun Rye...

584
00:31:18,504 --> 00:31:19,704
no, Ms. Park Su Nam...

585
00:31:19,774 --> 00:31:22,504
- is our landlord? - So?

586
00:31:23,844 --> 00:31:27,214
Did you know your mother was trying to kick my family out?

587
00:31:27,784 --> 00:31:28,784
What did you say?

588
00:31:30,584 --> 00:31:31,914
That old woman, really...

589
00:31:33,354 --> 00:31:34,754
She's telling you to move out?

590
00:31:36,084 --> 00:31:38,094
Han Gyu Rim broke up with you, right?

591
00:31:38,094 --> 00:31:39,524
So your mother is getting revenge, isn't she?

592
00:31:39,594 --> 00:31:42,064
No, we never even dated. How can we break up?

593
00:31:43,064 --> 00:31:44,364
You need to get Han Gyu Rim back.

594
00:31:44,434 --> 00:31:46,034
Tell her she gave you her body and soul...

595
00:31:46,094 --> 00:31:47,934
she gave you everything, so you have to take responsibility.

596
00:31:48,004 --> 00:31:49,164
Her body? We didn't...

597
00:31:49,804 --> 00:31:51,704
What? What did she give me?

598
00:31:51,804 --> 00:31:53,674
We haven't even really held hands.

599
00:31:54,644 --> 00:31:57,314
Are you from the Joseon Dynasty? Never mind.

600
00:31:57,414 --> 00:31:59,684
Just cling to her. Tell her, "I can't live without you."

601
00:31:59,744 --> 00:32:03,514
- "I'll just die." Threaten her. - Hey, you're the one...

602
00:32:03,714 --> 00:32:06,924
who made a huge scene telling me to stay away from your sister.

603
00:32:08,354 --> 00:32:09,994
That's because back then,

604
00:32:10,054 --> 00:32:12,124
I didn't know our landlord was the old lady, Park Su Nam.

605
00:32:13,324 --> 00:32:15,824
Here, let me see your head for a second.

606
00:32:16,494 --> 00:32:17,894
I'm going to pull out your gray hairs.

607
00:32:18,494 --> 00:32:20,864
I have gray hairs? Why would I have gray hairs already?

608
00:32:20,934 --> 00:32:21,934
That's so annoying.

609
00:32:24,204 --> 00:32:25,434
Darn it.

610
00:32:26,274 --> 00:32:27,604
Why did you hit me?

611
00:32:27,704 --> 00:32:31,774
You rotten little brat. Why did you have to be a girl?

612
00:32:32,414 --> 00:32:34,484
If you were a boy, I'd beat you for three days and nights...

613
00:32:34,544 --> 00:32:35,914
and then beat you again in the morning.

614
00:32:36,244 --> 00:32:37,254
Hey.

615
00:32:37,414 --> 00:32:41,254
Is Gyu Rim a coffee cup? A desk? A chair?

616
00:32:41,324 --> 00:32:43,024
Does she have no preferences? Is she incapable of thinking?

617
00:32:43,094 --> 00:32:44,094
Is she an inanimate object?

618
00:32:45,024 --> 00:32:47,464
Sim Cheong threw herself into the sea for her family.

619
00:32:47,524 --> 00:32:49,224
Can't she do this one thing for ours?

620
00:32:49,734 --> 00:32:50,864
If things work out with you,

621
00:32:50,934 --> 00:32:52,494
we'd never have to worry about a home.

622
00:32:52,564 --> 00:32:54,664
Why does only your sister have to be Sim Cheong?

623
00:32:55,364 --> 00:32:57,004
You be Sim Cheong, then.

624
00:32:57,074 --> 00:32:58,904
You'd never have to worry about a home.

625
00:32:59,004 --> 00:33:01,144
What? Dump your fiance.

626
00:33:01,444 --> 00:33:02,704
Marry me instead.

627
00:33:05,414 --> 00:33:08,284
Wait, do you like me? Or are you cursing me right now?

628
00:33:08,344 --> 00:33:09,884
Am I crazy?

629
00:33:09,954 --> 00:33:12,184
Right. You wouldn't want a guy like me...

630
00:33:12,254 --> 00:33:13,484
even if I came with a fortune, right?

631
00:33:13,684 --> 00:33:15,224
I wouldn't want a vixen like you...

632
00:33:15,284 --> 00:33:17,194
even with the 63 Building thrown in.

633
00:33:19,424 --> 00:33:21,464
If you say one more ridiculous thing,

634
00:33:21,524 --> 00:33:24,694
I'll tell your fiance all about the scam you pulled.

635
00:33:25,594 --> 00:33:27,234
I ought to just kick you.

636
00:33:30,334 --> 00:33:31,834
Darn it...

637
00:33:34,644 --> 00:33:35,774
Whatever.

638
00:33:36,144 --> 00:33:37,514
Even if they become beggars and live on the streets,

639
00:33:37,574 --> 00:33:39,314
why should I care?

640
00:33:42,484 --> 00:33:46,484
It's because I'm the one who'll suffer. Me.

641
00:33:47,554 --> 00:33:50,224
What if we all show up, begging her for help?

642
00:33:50,294 --> 00:33:51,294
I mean, what can she possibly do?

643
00:33:53,864 --> 00:33:56,694
I need to get Gyu Rim and Heung Sik together somehow...

644
00:33:57,034 --> 00:33:59,394
Is there really no way?

645
00:34:08,204 --> 00:34:10,314
I'll eat this to get my strength back,

646
00:34:11,574 --> 00:34:14,244
and I'll find a way to beat you and get out of here.

647
00:34:14,314 --> 00:34:15,344
You just watch.

648
00:34:19,824 --> 00:34:21,684
For every ten minutes that pass,

649
00:34:21,884 --> 00:34:24,224
I'll make things even harder on her.

650
00:34:25,494 --> 00:34:27,064
The longer this goes on,

651
00:34:27,164 --> 00:34:28,964
the harder it will be for your sister.

652
00:34:29,024 --> 00:34:30,364
If you understand that,

653
00:34:30,464 --> 00:34:31,634
you'd better get out of the way.

654
00:34:40,474 --> 00:34:42,804
Ma'am, until you've calmed down,

655
00:34:42,874 --> 00:34:44,644
can't you just yell at me and hit me instead?

656
00:34:44,774 --> 00:34:46,484
Can't you please go easy on my sister?

657
00:34:47,344 --> 00:34:49,984
I'd let her off, but she's the one who refuses.

658
00:34:51,084 --> 00:34:53,654
She says she'd rather die than take it back.

659
00:34:55,154 --> 00:34:56,184
I...

660
00:34:56,254 --> 00:34:58,754
I cared for her and liked her so much.

661
00:35:01,024 --> 00:35:03,394
I'm going to make her suffer as much as I used to like her.

662
00:35:03,734 --> 00:35:07,204
Exactly as much as I loved her, I'm going to make her suffer.

663
00:35:08,964 --> 00:35:09,974
Hey.

664
00:35:10,474 --> 00:35:13,404
The clock is ticking.

665
00:35:14,304 --> 00:35:17,314
Do you think I'll be stuck here forever?

666
00:35:18,814 --> 00:35:20,844
The more you and Heung Sik do this,

667
00:35:20,914 --> 00:35:22,844
the harder it will be on your sister.

668
00:35:26,314 --> 00:35:27,324
I know.

669
00:35:27,684 --> 00:35:30,354
Blocking you like this isn't going to solve anything.

670
00:35:30,824 --> 00:35:32,194
That's right. Of course.

671
00:35:32,254 --> 00:35:34,664
Well, now you're finally starting to make sense.

672
00:35:39,334 --> 00:35:40,664
What are you doing?

673
00:35:50,674 --> 00:35:51,674
Hey, Gyu Oh.

674
00:35:52,344 --> 00:35:55,084
Gyu Rim, I'm at Heung Sik's house.

675
00:35:56,114 --> 00:35:58,884
I'm stopping Ma'am from leaving right now.

676
00:35:59,284 --> 00:36:00,284
Why would you do that?

677
00:36:01,284 --> 00:36:03,554
Because I'm afraid Ma'am will leave and come harass you.

678
00:36:05,494 --> 00:36:06,864
Don't do that, Gyu Oh.

679
00:36:07,564 --> 00:36:08,794
Don't stop Ma'am.

680
00:36:09,794 --> 00:36:12,564
This is my problem. I'm the one who did wrong,

681
00:36:12,634 --> 00:36:13,934
and I'm the one who will fix it.

682
00:36:14,604 --> 00:36:15,904
Don't do this to Ma'am.

683
00:36:17,974 --> 00:36:18,974
Okay.

684
00:36:19,504 --> 00:36:20,944
You handle it, then. Okay?

685
00:36:22,344 --> 00:36:23,344
So?

686
00:36:25,244 --> 00:36:26,714
My sister says...

687
00:36:27,644 --> 00:36:30,354
- to let you go. - See?

688
00:36:30,414 --> 00:36:34,624
So your sister gets it now, right? The more you and Heung Sik do this,

689
00:36:34,684 --> 00:36:37,024
the more she's the one who suffers.

690
00:36:40,364 --> 00:36:41,564
But Ma'am...

691
00:36:42,624 --> 00:36:45,934
Why is the world so unfair to my sister?

692
00:36:46,194 --> 00:36:47,464
What's unfair about it?

693
00:36:48,004 --> 00:36:49,534
Whenever our family has a problem,

694
00:36:50,074 --> 00:36:51,074
whenever something happens,

695
00:36:51,134 --> 00:36:54,244
our sister Gyu Rim solves everything from start to finish.

696
00:36:56,344 --> 00:36:58,444
So why is there nothing we can do for her?

697
00:36:59,814 --> 00:37:01,244
Why is there nothing at all?

698
00:37:06,754 --> 00:37:08,924
No matter what nonsense you spout,

699
00:37:09,284 --> 00:37:11,824
I don't feel sorry for your sister one bit.

700
00:37:12,194 --> 00:37:14,464
If she made my child cry,

701
00:37:14,524 --> 00:37:18,034
then she should be crying tears of blood. That's what's fair.

702
00:37:18,564 --> 00:37:20,364
I'm leaving now. Thanks for your trouble.

703
00:37:20,434 --> 00:37:22,234
Eat this. It's really good.

704
00:37:28,144 --> 00:37:30,374
Yes. Jeongin Arcade, room 302?

705
00:37:30,674 --> 00:37:32,144
Yes, I understand.

706
00:37:32,544 --> 00:37:34,014
I'll have it delivered within the hour.

707
00:37:34,084 --> 00:37:35,214
Thank you.

708
00:37:38,154 --> 00:37:40,724
You're not scared of me at all, is that it?

709
00:37:44,424 --> 00:37:47,824
- Ma'am, you are here. - No matter how badly I treat you,

710
00:37:47,894 --> 00:37:49,294
you're not scared one bit.

711
00:37:49,624 --> 00:37:51,794
You're telling me to bring it on, is that it?

712
00:37:52,034 --> 00:37:55,634
- That's not it, Ma'am. - Right. Let's see about that.

713
00:37:56,434 --> 00:38:00,174
You'll find out just how scary and vicious I can be.

714
00:38:00,374 --> 00:38:02,574
Then you can be the third person to experience it.

715
00:38:03,074 --> 00:38:04,144
For your information,

716
00:38:04,314 --> 00:38:06,744
the first person who crossed me...

717
00:38:06,814 --> 00:38:09,214
was so scared of me, they moved abroad.

718
00:38:10,354 --> 00:38:14,924
The second one said they'd rather be in jail,

719
00:38:15,124 --> 00:38:17,524
and that's where they are right now.

720
00:38:20,364 --> 00:38:22,224
So where are you going to run?

721
00:38:22,664 --> 00:38:24,764
You'd better start thinking about it now, got it?

722
00:38:27,704 --> 00:38:30,334
Good grief, this is so salty, isn't it?

723
00:38:30,534 --> 00:38:32,234
Why is it this salty?

724
00:38:40,044 --> 00:38:41,314
I thought it tasted...

725
00:38:43,084 --> 00:38:44,084
fine.

726
00:38:44,254 --> 00:38:46,554
What do you mean, fine? Fine, my foot.

727
00:38:46,984 --> 00:38:48,284
Since you season everything like this,

728
00:38:48,354 --> 00:38:51,454
that's why customers don't buy what you make, right?

729
00:38:52,454 --> 00:38:55,694
I've been holding my tongue so I wouldn't discourage you.

730
00:38:56,394 --> 00:38:59,734
But the seasoned greens and side dishes you make...

731
00:38:59,934 --> 00:39:02,334
Do you have any idea how many complaints I've gotten?

732
00:39:02,834 --> 00:39:04,834
Everyone says the kimchi I make is delicious.

733
00:39:04,904 --> 00:39:06,604
The praise is endless, you know?

734
00:39:07,604 --> 00:39:09,674
But every single customer says the same thing...

735
00:39:09,874 --> 00:39:12,514
that they could make it better themselves.

736
00:39:13,114 --> 00:39:14,714
They ask why I keep an employee with no talent...

737
00:39:14,784 --> 00:39:18,054
and haven't fired you already.

738
00:39:20,024 --> 00:39:21,024
What's this?

739
00:39:21,724 --> 00:39:22,754
What's that look for?

740
00:39:23,454 --> 00:39:26,254
That's the look of someone who feels wronged, right?

741
00:39:27,264 --> 00:39:30,594
That look says, "But my side dishes sell just fine."

742
00:39:30,934 --> 00:39:34,234
A look that's arguing and protesting against me, right?

743
00:39:36,504 --> 00:39:38,034
If you feel so wronged, then leave, you hear?

744
00:39:38,204 --> 00:39:41,274
I won't stop you, so just quit and get out.

745
00:39:42,404 --> 00:39:43,444
I'm sorry.

746
00:39:43,814 --> 00:39:46,714
I'll be more careful and do a better job from now on.

747
00:39:47,984 --> 00:39:51,414
What "from now on?" You're about to be fired.

748
00:39:52,254 --> 00:39:53,254
And...

749
00:39:53,314 --> 00:39:56,254
From now on,

750
00:39:56,824 --> 00:39:58,924
buy whole heads of garlic, not the peeled cloves.

751
00:39:58,994 --> 00:40:01,664
We're going to peel them all one by one,

752
00:40:01,724 --> 00:40:03,164
so you can do it yourself, got it?

753
00:40:05,334 --> 00:40:06,804
What, you can't do it?

754
00:40:08,204 --> 00:40:10,674
I said quit if you have a problem with it.

755
00:40:11,974 --> 00:40:15,274
No, I have no problem with it. I'll peel them all myself.

756
00:40:15,344 --> 00:40:16,504
The garlic. Whole heads.

757
00:40:19,514 --> 00:40:21,144
Good, then. Right.

758
00:40:21,744 --> 00:40:23,784
Order the whole garlic right now.

759
00:40:24,184 --> 00:40:25,184
Yes.

760
00:40:29,954 --> 00:40:34,894
(Suragan Side Dishes)

761
00:40:42,134 --> 00:40:44,074
Oh my, is the bell broken?

762
00:40:44,574 --> 00:40:46,974
Oh, my. When did you come in, ma'am?

763
00:40:47,504 --> 00:40:50,274
You look like a new customer.

764
00:40:50,944 --> 00:40:52,644
We have lots of delicious side dishes,

765
00:40:52,714 --> 00:40:54,214
so take your time and have a look.

766
00:40:55,014 --> 00:40:56,014
Yes.

767
00:41:00,784 --> 00:41:02,684
Welcome. Please, feel free to look around.

768
00:41:03,524 --> 00:41:05,424
You didn't even know the bell was broken?

769
00:41:05,824 --> 00:41:07,424
My goodness.

770
00:41:07,594 --> 00:41:09,124
It was working this morning.

771
00:41:09,464 --> 00:41:12,094
Where is your head at? Honestly.

772
00:41:12,594 --> 00:41:14,834
I'll fix it as soon as I get back from my delivery.

773
00:41:15,234 --> 00:41:16,434
The more I dislike you,

774
00:41:16,504 --> 00:41:18,574
the more you do things to make me dislike you.

775
00:41:19,174 --> 00:41:20,374
I'll be back.

776
00:41:27,814 --> 00:41:29,244
The person who just left...

777
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:31,514
Was that Han Gyu Rim?

778
00:41:34,584 --> 00:41:37,554
Yes, it was. Why do you ask?

779
00:41:40,324 --> 00:41:42,624
Seeing how you were scolding her,

780
00:41:43,124 --> 00:41:45,034
she must have done something awful.

781
00:41:46,194 --> 00:41:48,564
You didn't come to buy side dishes.

782
00:41:49,004 --> 00:41:50,974
Did you come to see Han Gyu Rim?

783
00:41:52,074 --> 00:41:54,004
No, I came to buy side dishes.

784
00:41:56,204 --> 00:41:58,444
Could I possibly try some of the kimchi?

785
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:01,444
Of course. Just wait a moment.

786
00:42:07,554 --> 00:42:08,554
This kimchi...

787
00:42:09,124 --> 00:42:11,424
You make this yourself, right, ma'am?

788
00:42:11,824 --> 00:42:13,964
I don't let anyone else make the kimchi.

789
00:42:14,524 --> 00:42:16,424
When it comes to my kimchi,

790
00:42:16,694 --> 00:42:20,664
I'm second to none in all of Korea. That's how proud I am of it.

791
00:42:20,964 --> 00:42:23,034
Here, have a taste.

792
00:42:29,944 --> 00:42:30,944
It's salty.

793
00:42:31,814 --> 00:42:32,814
Salty?

794
00:42:33,344 --> 00:42:35,084
That can't be right.

795
00:42:39,584 --> 00:42:41,254
How is this salty?

796
00:42:41,484 --> 00:42:43,524
Are you arguing with me?

797
00:42:44,694 --> 00:42:47,894
- No, I'm not arguing... - It's salty to me.

798
00:42:49,024 --> 00:42:52,134
You must prefer your food very bland.

799
00:42:52,564 --> 00:42:55,404
Then try this radish kimchi.

800
00:42:55,734 --> 00:42:59,234
I made this radish kimchi for the Seoul palate,

801
00:42:59,304 --> 00:43:01,274
so it's perfectly mild.

802
00:43:01,344 --> 00:43:02,444
Go on, try it.

803
00:43:09,614 --> 00:43:10,614
Bitter.

804
00:43:10,884 --> 00:43:14,154
- Bitter? - You call this radish kimchi?

805
00:43:14,884 --> 00:43:17,054
Even I could make it better than this.

806
00:43:22,124 --> 00:43:23,124
Sour.

807
00:43:23,764 --> 00:43:26,134
How can green onion kimchi be this sour?

808
00:43:26,264 --> 00:43:27,964
I wouldn't eat this even if it were free.

809
00:43:29,534 --> 00:43:31,104
Then don't buy it.

810
00:43:31,774 --> 00:43:34,304
I have no intention of selling to a customer like you anyway,

811
00:43:34,574 --> 00:43:36,474
so get out of here this instant.

812
00:43:38,014 --> 00:43:39,374
In my 30 years of running this shop,

813
00:43:39,444 --> 00:43:42,114
I've never been so insulted in my life. Honestly.

814
00:43:43,114 --> 00:43:46,254
So I'm spending my own money,

815
00:43:46,514 --> 00:43:48,284
and I'm not allowed to say it's salty, bitter, or sour?

816
00:43:48,654 --> 00:43:51,254
There's something wrong with your taste buds,

817
00:43:51,324 --> 00:43:53,324
so why are you blaming my kimchi?

818
00:43:53,494 --> 00:43:55,424
How dare you wound my pride?

819
00:43:55,424 --> 00:43:56,424
- Get out. - Oh my.

820
00:43:56,424 --> 00:43:59,764
I wouldn't take your money if you offered me a fortune.

821
00:43:59,834 --> 00:44:01,834
- Get out right now. - You old hag.

822
00:44:01,904 --> 00:44:03,034
Get out.

823
00:44:03,364 --> 00:44:06,804
What kind of a shop is this? I ought to report you.

824
00:44:07,504 --> 00:44:08,904
Go ahead, report me. Report me.

825
00:44:09,244 --> 00:44:11,974
I'm not scared one bit, so report me all you want.

826
00:44:14,714 --> 00:44:16,514
You don't look like you're from around here,

827
00:44:16,584 --> 00:44:19,314
so don't ever come near this place again.

828
00:44:20,214 --> 00:44:22,784
Gosh, that old hag.

829
00:44:24,524 --> 00:44:25,524
Are you okay?

830
00:44:25,824 --> 00:44:26,924
Yes.

831
00:44:27,394 --> 00:44:29,224
- Goodness. - Let me help you up.

832
00:44:29,294 --> 00:44:31,134
No, no, I'm fine.

833
00:44:35,634 --> 00:44:37,004
Unbelievable.

834
00:44:37,674 --> 00:44:40,674
Excuse me, is there a pharmacy or, no,

835
00:44:41,674 --> 00:44:43,474
is there a convenience store around here?

836
00:44:44,514 --> 00:44:45,874
If you leave the shopping arcade...

837
00:44:45,944 --> 00:44:47,884
and turn right, you'll see a rice cake shop.

838
00:44:47,944 --> 00:44:48,944
From there...

839
00:44:51,154 --> 00:44:52,384
Actually, just follow me.

840
00:44:52,914 --> 00:44:53,924
You're able to walk, right?

841
00:44:54,324 --> 00:44:55,884
Yes, of course.

842
00:45:00,424 --> 00:45:02,124
I can't believe she has to work there,

843
00:45:02,424 --> 00:45:05,134
taking that kind of abuse from that old hag.

844
00:45:06,864 --> 00:45:09,534
Han Gyu Rim, what is wrong with you?

845
00:45:13,804 --> 00:45:16,504
They said there's a restroom behind the building.

846
00:45:16,574 --> 00:45:18,844
And you can change your stockings in there.

847
00:45:19,614 --> 00:45:21,814
Do you need me to buy you a pain relief patch?

848
00:45:22,214 --> 00:45:24,514
No, that's all right. This is plenty.

849
00:45:25,614 --> 00:45:26,614
Are you in high school?

850
00:45:27,014 --> 00:45:31,694
- Yes. - You're one of a kind these days.

851
00:45:32,024 --> 00:45:34,194
Your parents must have raised you well.

852
00:45:35,524 --> 00:45:38,034
If you do not need anything else, I will get going.

853
00:45:38,464 --> 00:45:39,464
Okay.

854
00:45:39,534 --> 00:45:41,504
I have taken up too much of your time, haven't I?

855
00:45:42,204 --> 00:45:43,234
Wait a minute.

856
00:45:43,634 --> 00:45:45,704
Oh, this is all the cash I have on me.

857
00:45:45,774 --> 00:45:48,244
- Go buy yourself a snack. - No, that is okay.

858
00:45:48,774 --> 00:45:51,814
- Get well soon. - Come on, just take it.

859
00:45:52,714 --> 00:45:53,714
Thank you.

860
00:45:56,944 --> 00:45:59,384
His mother must be so proud of him.

861
00:46:01,684 --> 00:46:03,654
I wish I had a son like that.

862
00:46:05,994 --> 00:46:08,564
Oh my, did that student leave this behind?

863
00:46:11,264 --> 00:46:12,264
Oh, dear.

864
00:46:13,234 --> 00:46:15,234
I should have at least asked his name.

865
00:46:21,044 --> 00:46:22,704
That crazy old hag.

866
00:46:23,204 --> 00:46:25,014
How am I going to get my revenge?

867
00:46:28,814 --> 00:46:32,114
How is she going to get revenge on that crazy old bat?

868
00:46:32,654 --> 00:46:34,954
The more I think about it, the angrier I get.

869
00:46:35,384 --> 00:46:39,294
I'm so furious I can barely breathe.

870
00:46:40,594 --> 00:46:41,594
Grandma.

871
00:46:42,764 --> 00:46:44,934
Oh. Your sister is not here. Go away.

872
00:46:45,194 --> 00:46:47,364
I am not here to see my sister. I came to buy some curry.

873
00:46:48,804 --> 00:46:50,264
You came to buy curry?

874
00:46:50,634 --> 00:46:53,104
I was really craving the curry my older sister makes.

875
00:46:54,104 --> 00:46:56,274
What? Did your sister...

876
00:46:56,344 --> 00:46:59,074
tell you to come here and buy her food?

877
00:46:59,514 --> 00:47:01,344
You can just ask your sister to make it for you.

878
00:47:01,414 --> 00:47:02,984
Why come all the way here to buy it?

879
00:47:03,144 --> 00:47:04,214
From now on,

880
00:47:04,284 --> 00:47:05,754
we have decided to each make our own food.

881
00:47:07,924 --> 00:47:09,684
What are you talking about?

882
00:47:09,824 --> 00:47:12,454
It means Gyu Rim is going to stop worrying about the family,

883
00:47:12,654 --> 00:47:15,064
eat what she wants to eat, and do what she wants to do.

884
00:47:15,664 --> 00:47:16,894
That is how we decided she will live now.

885
00:47:17,634 --> 00:47:20,064
What? Why? Why all of a sudden?

886
00:47:21,234 --> 00:47:23,834
Because the most important person to Gyu Rim...

887
00:47:24,574 --> 00:47:25,834
is herself.

888
00:47:27,274 --> 00:47:29,004
So you are saying your sister,

889
00:47:29,644 --> 00:47:31,644
to use the slang kids use these days,

890
00:47:32,914 --> 00:47:34,544
has had an "awakening?"

891
00:47:36,144 --> 00:47:37,144
I guess so.

892
00:47:37,654 --> 00:47:39,084
I had not thought of it that way.

893
00:47:39,184 --> 00:47:40,184
It seems my older sister...

894
00:47:40,254 --> 00:47:41,254
really has had an awakening, Grandma.

895
00:47:42,454 --> 00:47:44,024
You are the one who has had an awakening.

896
00:47:49,694 --> 00:47:53,064
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

897
00:47:53,664 --> 00:47:55,634
Where are you?

898
00:47:56,264 --> 00:47:57,734
Mu Jin.

899
00:47:58,334 --> 00:48:00,374
Kim Mu Jin.

900
00:48:01,244 --> 00:48:03,744
Where are you?

901
00:48:04,714 --> 00:48:08,844
Kim Mu Jin. Where are you?

902
00:48:09,684 --> 00:48:11,254
Mu Jin.

903
00:48:11,854 --> 00:48:13,214
Kim Mu Jin.

904
00:48:13,984 --> 00:48:17,624
Where are you? Mu Jin.

905
00:48:18,194 --> 00:48:20,394
Mu Jin.

906
00:48:24,164 --> 00:48:25,964
Mu Jin.

907
00:48:26,634 --> 00:48:28,364
Mu Jin.

908
00:48:29,034 --> 00:48:30,974
Kim Mu Jin.

909
00:48:31,834 --> 00:48:33,474
Kim Mu Jin.

910
00:48:34,174 --> 00:48:36,804
Where are you?

911
00:48:38,544 --> 00:48:41,744
- Mu Jin. - Did you lose someone?

912
00:48:42,614 --> 00:48:43,844
My little brother.

913
00:48:44,584 --> 00:48:45,584
Oh no.

914
00:48:46,184 --> 00:48:47,354
How old is your brother?

915
00:48:47,824 --> 00:48:49,454
He's nine.

916
00:48:50,654 --> 00:48:53,094
Where's your mom? Did you call the police?

917
00:48:53,794 --> 00:48:56,164
My mom went to work.

918
00:48:56,564 --> 00:49:00,464
I wanted to look for him myself before calling them.

919
00:49:05,574 --> 00:49:09,344
Don't cry. It's okay. I'll help you look for him.

920
00:49:10,244 --> 00:49:11,674
What does Mu Jin look like?

921
00:49:11,944 --> 00:49:13,214
What colour clothes is he wearing today...

922
00:49:13,274 --> 00:49:16,284
Do you have a picture of Mu Jin, by any chance?

923
00:49:16,644 --> 00:49:18,914
I have a picture of Mu Jin.

924
00:49:31,934 --> 00:49:34,004
Mu Jin is so adorable.

925
00:49:34,904 --> 00:49:36,834
I'll look over that way,

926
00:49:36,904 --> 00:49:38,134
so you look over there.

927
00:49:39,074 --> 00:49:41,944
I'll put my number in your phone, so save it,

928
00:49:42,304 --> 00:49:43,804
and we'll let each other know if we find him.

929
00:49:46,814 --> 00:49:47,814
Here.

930
00:49:49,414 --> 00:49:52,254
My name is Kim Mu Gyeong.

931
00:49:53,284 --> 00:49:56,424
Okay, Mu Gyeong. We'll definitely find Mu Jin.

932
00:49:57,124 --> 00:49:58,124
Don't you worry.

933
00:50:03,794 --> 00:50:05,234
Mu Jin.

934
00:50:06,264 --> 00:50:07,504
Kim Mu Jin.

935
00:50:09,834 --> 00:50:11,134
Mu Jin.

936
00:50:12,734 --> 00:50:14,174
Kim Mu Jin.

937
00:50:15,304 --> 00:50:18,044
Excuse me, have you seen a puppy that looks like this?

938
00:50:19,544 --> 00:50:22,414
He's white, and his name is Mu Jin.

939
00:50:24,314 --> 00:50:25,454
Mu Jin.

940
00:50:26,854 --> 00:50:28,054
Kim Mu Jin.

941
00:50:31,094 --> 00:50:32,394
Mu Jin.

942
00:50:33,854 --> 00:50:35,094
Kim Mu Jin.

943
00:50:38,094 --> 00:50:39,334
Mu Jin.

944
00:50:40,034 --> 00:50:41,604
Kim Mu Jin.

945
00:50:42,604 --> 00:50:45,874
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

946
00:50:47,774 --> 00:50:49,244
Mu Jin.

947
00:50:51,114 --> 00:50:52,744
Kim Mu Jin.

948
00:50:58,454 --> 00:50:59,454
Did you hear that?

949
00:50:59,614 --> 00:51:00,614
Hear what?

950
00:51:01,354 --> 00:51:02,524
Someone calling my name.

951
00:51:02,854 --> 00:51:04,424
What are you talking about?

952
00:51:05,654 --> 00:51:07,054
I don't hear a thing.

953
00:51:08,624 --> 00:51:09,764
I definitely heard it.

954
00:51:11,164 --> 00:51:12,164
Who?

955
00:51:12,464 --> 00:51:13,464
The grim reaper?

956
00:51:15,034 --> 00:51:16,764
No, Gyu Rim.

957
00:51:25,044 --> 00:51:27,244
I didn't sleep well last night.

958
00:51:28,414 --> 00:51:29,414
Sorry.

959
00:51:30,184 --> 00:51:31,584
I'm going to go splash some cold water on my face.

960
00:51:37,354 --> 00:51:38,524
Make it ice water.

961
00:51:41,424 --> 00:51:42,464
Mu Jin.

962
00:51:45,264 --> 00:51:46,634
Kim Mu Jin.

963
00:51:49,404 --> 00:51:50,634
Mu Jin.

964
00:51:54,304 --> 00:51:55,644
Kim Mu Jin.

965
00:52:06,054 --> 00:52:07,754
Are you Mu Jin?

966
00:52:14,564 --> 00:52:15,564
Come here.

967
00:52:15,924 --> 00:52:19,334
Your sister's going crazy looking for you.

968
00:52:20,934 --> 00:52:21,934
Let me see.

969
00:52:23,034 --> 00:52:24,034
It is you.

970
00:52:25,374 --> 00:52:27,074
You are Mu Jin.

971
00:52:32,114 --> 00:52:33,774
I found you, Kim Mu Jin.

972
00:52:37,284 --> 00:52:38,284
I found you.

973
00:52:50,024 --> 00:52:52,734
Come on, Kim Mu Jin. Get a grip.

974
00:52:53,234 --> 00:52:54,364
Get a grip.

975
00:53:17,484 --> 00:53:18,494
Yes?

976
00:53:19,224 --> 00:53:20,864
Is this Han Gyu Oh's phone?

977
00:53:22,194 --> 00:53:23,194
Yes, it is.

978
00:53:24,294 --> 00:53:26,934
Hello. This is Min Ju. Kwon Hee Na's friend.

979
00:53:27,634 --> 00:53:29,664
Oh, hello.

980
00:53:30,764 --> 00:53:33,234
I need to discuss something with you about Hee Na.

981
00:53:33,804 --> 00:53:35,344
Can we meet for a minute?

982
00:53:36,044 --> 00:53:37,644
Did something happen to Hee Na?

983
00:53:38,244 --> 00:53:39,244
Is she sick?

984
00:53:39,714 --> 00:53:41,284
I'll tell you when we meet.

985
00:53:55,294 --> 00:53:56,294
What's going on?

986
00:53:57,294 --> 00:53:58,494
Please, have a seat.

987
00:53:58,734 --> 00:53:59,794
Just tell me what it is.

988
00:54:01,904 --> 00:54:03,764
I'll tell you once you sit down.

989
00:54:12,574 --> 00:54:15,214
- What would you like to drink? - What happened to Hee Na?

990
00:54:16,084 --> 00:54:17,084
Tell me that first.

991
00:54:23,154 --> 00:54:24,694
Nothing happened to Hee Na.

992
00:54:25,524 --> 00:54:26,724
I lied.

993
00:54:31,564 --> 00:54:33,694
You wouldn't have come if I'd been the one to ask, would you?

994
00:54:39,104 --> 00:54:41,974
Hee Na said she isn't interested in you.

995
00:54:42,544 --> 00:54:43,844
That's why she didn't show up.

996
00:54:47,784 --> 00:54:48,784
I see.

997
00:54:50,184 --> 00:54:53,514
She told me I should give it a shot with you.

998
00:54:57,424 --> 00:54:58,794
As far as I know,

999
00:54:59,494 --> 00:55:00,964
you're Su Chan's girlfriend.

1000
00:55:05,034 --> 00:55:06,834
I broke up with Su Chan a little while ago.

1001
00:55:07,634 --> 00:55:10,634
I hate cheating.

1002
00:55:14,804 --> 00:55:16,904
Stop clinging to someone who isn't interested...

1003
00:55:17,304 --> 00:55:18,614
and just date me.

1004
00:55:19,174 --> 00:55:20,474
Once you start seeing me,

1005
00:55:20,774 --> 00:55:22,744
you'll forget a girl like Kwon Hee Na in no time.

1006
00:55:26,384 --> 00:55:27,454
Excuse me, but...

1007
00:55:29,424 --> 00:55:32,424
I have a policy of not engaging with psychos like you.

1008
00:55:33,854 --> 00:55:36,494
Have an iced americano with extra ice...

1009
00:55:36,894 --> 00:55:37,894
and snap out of it.

1010
00:55:42,804 --> 00:55:43,804
Han Gyu Oh.

1011
00:55:49,974 --> 00:55:50,974
Wait, what?

1012
00:55:51,914 --> 00:55:53,674
He's so much sexier when he's angry.

1013
00:55:55,584 --> 00:55:58,284
There's no way I can give up on you now.

1014
00:56:15,134 --> 00:56:16,734
Did Min Ju really say that?

1015
00:56:17,304 --> 00:56:19,534
That she wants to break up with you and date Han Gyu Oh?

1016
00:56:19,904 --> 00:56:21,974
She said she told you too.

1017
00:56:22,474 --> 00:56:23,474
That little...

1018
00:56:24,144 --> 00:56:25,644
Is she crazy?

1019
00:56:29,344 --> 00:56:30,984
She seems crazy to us,

1020
00:56:32,154 --> 00:56:34,054
but Min Ju doesn't think she is.

1021
00:56:34,384 --> 00:56:36,654
She thinks she's just being honest about her feelings.

1022
00:56:36,724 --> 00:56:38,554
Still, does this make any sense?

1023
00:56:42,924 --> 00:56:44,124
I'm the idiot.

1024
00:56:44,194 --> 00:56:46,294
I never should have let her meet Han Gyu Oh.

1025
00:56:46,434 --> 00:56:48,904
Seriously, how could you be so thoughtless?

1026
00:56:49,264 --> 00:56:51,104
Everyone knows Min Ju is a sucker for a pretty face.

1027
00:56:51,274 --> 00:56:52,834
Couldn't you predict she'd go crazy for him?

1028
00:56:53,034 --> 00:56:57,644
Han Gyu Oh is handsome enough to make anyone's head turn.

1029
00:56:57,974 --> 00:57:00,844
If you put a fish in front of a cat, what do you expect to happen?

1030
00:57:01,014 --> 00:57:03,214
How could you date her for so long and not even realise that?

1031
00:57:03,284 --> 00:57:05,354
How could you cause so much trouble for everyone?

1032
00:57:06,014 --> 00:57:07,784
No, I just...

1033
00:57:09,424 --> 00:57:12,224
I just wanted to set Gyu Oh up with you.

1034
00:57:13,994 --> 00:57:17,224
I just assumed you'd like Gyu Oh too.

1035
00:57:18,294 --> 00:57:20,534
So you're saying this is my fault?

1036
00:57:21,734 --> 00:57:23,304
Then why not Han Gyu Oh?

1037
00:57:23,864 --> 00:57:25,804
Like you said, he's insanely handsome and cool...

1038
00:57:25,874 --> 00:57:27,304
and ridiculously charming.

1039
00:57:27,674 --> 00:57:29,874
Honestly, if you had just liked Gyu Oh,

1040
00:57:30,104 --> 00:57:31,614
this whole thing would be solved.

1041
00:57:32,744 --> 00:57:34,514
Honestly,

1042
00:57:35,314 --> 00:57:36,844
aren't you the one causing all the trouble?

1043
00:58:01,844 --> 00:58:04,344
(Mu Gyeong)

1044
00:58:04,674 --> 00:58:05,714
Hi.

1045
00:58:06,374 --> 00:58:07,614
So you're Mu Jin.

1046
00:58:07,844 --> 00:58:11,484
Thanks to you, ma'am, our Mu Jin is healthy and doing well.

1047
00:58:12,184 --> 00:58:14,784
That's a relief. I'm so glad.

1048
00:58:15,254 --> 00:58:18,454
Mu Jin, you should thank the lady.

1049
00:58:19,054 --> 00:58:21,724
Mu Jin, don't get lost again...

1050
00:58:21,864 --> 00:58:24,464
and live happily with your mom and sister.

1051
00:58:24,764 --> 00:58:26,164
Thank you.

1052
00:58:26,664 --> 00:58:28,004
Bye.

1053
00:58:28,134 --> 00:58:29,464
Bye, Mu Gyeong.

1054
00:58:30,704 --> 00:58:31,704
Bye.

1055
00:58:32,434 --> 00:58:33,504
Kim Mu Jin.

1056
00:58:39,744 --> 00:58:41,074
Thank you, Kim Mu Jin.

1057
00:58:42,344 --> 00:58:44,714
Thanks to you, at least I got to say his name over and over.

1058
00:59:06,274 --> 00:59:07,404
I can't take it anymore.

1059
00:59:09,404 --> 00:59:11,414
I can't take it, even if I'm damned for it.

1060
00:59:27,794 --> 00:59:28,794
Welcome.

1061
00:59:29,624 --> 00:59:30,864
Are you here for a meal?

1062
00:59:31,734 --> 00:59:32,734
Yes.

1063
00:59:36,964 --> 00:59:38,004
I've got this.

1064
00:59:40,404 --> 00:59:42,304
What brings you here?

1065
00:59:42,704 --> 00:59:45,174
Our Mu Jin is extremely busy right now.

1066
00:59:48,914 --> 00:59:50,384
I came here to eat.

1067
00:59:51,684 --> 00:59:52,684
Excuse me?

1068
00:59:56,054 --> 00:59:57,724
This is a restaurant, isn't it?

1069
01:00:01,594 --> 01:00:02,594
Right.

1070
01:00:04,164 --> 01:00:06,234
Well, please have a seat at that empty table for now.

1071
01:00:16,444 --> 01:00:18,044
Here's the menu.

1072
01:00:26,114 --> 01:00:27,654
I'll have the kimchi fried rice.

1073
01:00:29,954 --> 01:00:32,594
We don't have kimchi fried rice on the menu.

1074
01:00:58,184 --> 01:01:01,114
Hey, can you make kimchi fried rice?

1075
01:01:02,484 --> 01:01:04,184
Kimchi fried rice? Out of the blue?

1076
01:01:08,394 --> 01:01:09,394
So that's a no?

1077
01:01:09,764 --> 01:01:10,864
I'll make it for you at home.

1078
01:01:11,594 --> 01:01:14,334
Not at home. A customer wants it.

1079
01:01:15,734 --> 01:01:17,704
Tell them to order something from the menu.

1080
01:01:17,964 --> 01:01:19,234
I already told them that.

1081
01:01:22,074 --> 01:01:23,174
Who's the customer?

1082
01:01:29,044 --> 01:01:30,084
An elderly person?

1083
01:01:33,714 --> 01:01:35,384
Not an elderly person.

1084
01:01:36,524 --> 01:01:37,854
Then tell them to order from the menu.

1085
01:01:49,134 --> 01:01:50,264
What is it?

1086
01:01:52,774 --> 01:01:53,804
Something's going on, isn't it?

1087
01:01:54,434 --> 01:01:55,974
Why am I such a softy?

1088
01:01:56,044 --> 01:01:57,974
Especially with children, women, and the elderly.

1089
01:01:58,574 --> 01:02:00,744
So who ordered the kimchi fried rice?

1090
01:02:01,714 --> 01:02:02,714
A child?

1091
01:02:04,854 --> 01:02:05,854
A woman?

1092
01:02:07,154 --> 01:02:08,354
Another woman who's your type?

1093
01:02:09,784 --> 01:02:10,884
Gosh.

1094
01:02:11,394 --> 01:02:13,124
Just tell her to order something from the menu.

1095
01:02:13,894 --> 01:02:16,064
Or you go over there and say, "You're just my type."

1096
01:02:16,124 --> 01:02:17,964
"Would you like to have kimchi fried rice with me?"

1097
01:02:18,164 --> 01:02:19,464
You should go ask her yourself.

1098
01:02:22,504 --> 01:02:24,664
The woman who's so my type is Han Gyu Rim.

1099
01:02:27,774 --> 01:02:29,004
It's not like you're getting back together.

1100
01:02:29,074 --> 01:02:30,844
It's just one plate of kimchi fried rice.

1101
01:02:32,014 --> 01:02:33,144
You can make that for her, can't you?

1102
01:04:21,454 --> 01:04:22,724
There's kimchi in the fridge, right?

1103
01:04:23,054 --> 01:04:24,054
Yes.

1104
01:04:51,484 --> 01:04:53,184
(Love on the Menu)

1105
01:04:53,654 --> 01:04:56,784
Forget about your wedding. Just call the whole thing off.

1106
01:04:56,854 --> 01:04:58,524
No matter what, I'm getting married.

1107
01:04:58,594 --> 01:05:00,424
The girl you said was seeing Mu Jin...

1108
01:05:01,024 --> 01:05:02,064
that girl...

1109
01:05:02,394 --> 01:05:03,624
She's my daughter.

1110
01:05:04,564 --> 01:05:05,694
What happened to your face?

1111
01:05:06,264 --> 01:05:08,734
- Have you been crying? - My mom is type O,

1112
01:05:08,804 --> 01:05:11,734
- but I'm type AB. - Gyeol, where are you?

1113
01:05:12,034 --> 01:05:13,134
This is Kim Mu Jin.

1114
01:05:13,504 --> 01:05:15,874
So who's my mom then?

1115
01:05:16,844 --> 01:05:19,244
And who is my dad?

